1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,640
The French Revolution, explained like you are five.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:06,280
Step one, in 1789, France is broke.

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:09,920
Decades of wars, a lavish royal court at Versailles,

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,440
bad harvests, the country is bankrupt,

5
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:14,200
and the people are starving.

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,200
King Louis XVI calls a meeting of the Estates General

7
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,600
for the first time in 175 years.

8
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,400
The three Estates, the clergy, the nobility,

9
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,880
and everyone else, everyone else is 97% of France,

10
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:30,200
and they have exactly one vote.

11
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:33,200
The same as the clergy, the same as the nobility,

12
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,880
so the 97% walk out and form their own assembly.

13
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:40,280
Step two, Louis panics and locks them out

14
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,680
of their meeting hall,

15
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,000
so they gather at a nearby tennis court

16
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,320
and swear an oath not to leave

17
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:47,600
until France has a constitution.

18
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:48,960
Louis backs down.

19
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,720
But in Paris, the rumor spreads

20
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:54,280
that the king is gathering troops to crush the assembly.

21
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:59,280
On July 14, 1789, the people of Paris storm the Bastille.

22
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:03,680
The Bastille is a royal prison, a symbol of royal tyranny.

23
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:06,840
There are exactly seven prisoners inside when they take it.

24
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:09,320
The symbol matters more than what's in it.

25
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:13,560
Step three, the revolution spreads across France like fire.

26
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:15,440
Nobles flee the country.

27
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,200
The church loses its land.

28
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,560
Feudalism is abolished overnight.

29
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:23,600
In 1791, France gets its first constitution.

30
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:27,160
Louis is still king, but his power is now limited.

31
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,080
And here's the thing.

32
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:30,600
Louis tries to flee France in disguise.

33
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,960
He is recognized at a small town called Varen,

34
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,440
brought back to Paris in humiliation,

35
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:38,960
and the trust gone forever.

36
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:42,880
Step four, in 1792, France declares war

37
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:44,320
on Austria and Prussia.

38
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:46,640
The foreign powers want to crush the revolution

39
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:48,640
before it spreads to their own countries.

40
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,400
The war goes badly at first.

41
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,720
Paris panics.

42
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:53,760
Radical revolutionaries take over.

43
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:55,840
Louis is arrested, tried for treason,

44
00:01:55,840 --> 00:02:00,720
and executed by guillotine on January 21, 1793.

45
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:03,000
The crowd cheers the revolution,

46
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,160
no longer interested in a constitutional monarchy.

47
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,880
Now it wants a republic,

48
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,880
and it is willing to kill anyone who disagrees.

49
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:14,880
Step five, what follows is called the reign of terror.

50
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,520
A revolutionary committee called

51
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,320
the Committee of Public Safety takes control,

52
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:21,960
led by Maximilien Robespierre.

53
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:24,680
Anyone suspected of being an enemy of the revolution

54
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:28,800
is arrested, suspected, not convicted, suspected.

55
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,360
17,000 people are officially executed.

56
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:34,920
Perhaps 40,000 die in prison or without trial.

57
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:37,120
Robespierre signs the death warrants.

58
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,680
He calls it necessary.

59
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,880
He calls it virtue.

60
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:44,880
Step six, in July 1794, Robespierre himself is arrested

61
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,880
by the same men who helped him arrest everyone else.

62
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:49,960
They are afraid they are next.

63
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:52,600
He is guillotined the following day.

64
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,320
The instrument of the revolution

65
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:57,120
used on the revolution's own leader.

66
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:59,240
Napoleon Bonaparte watches all of this

67
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:01,640
from a distance, takes careful notes,

68
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:06,320
and in 1799 walks into the chaos and takes power.

69
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,320
The revolution that promised liberty,

70
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:12,760
equality, and fraternity ends with a military dictatorship.

71
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,600
The idea survives.

72
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,400
The execution consumed itself,

73
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:20,760
and that's just one story inside Paladin.

74
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,480
It's like Duolingo, but for history lovers.

75
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:26,160
Download it now and become the most intelligent person

76
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,000
in the room.

